# Slurm submit files and shell scripts execute on Linux compute nodes.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this checkout, so without these rules a .sub file
# lands on Windows with CRLF endings, gets copied to HPC3, and fails there with
# "/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory" -- an error that
# names neither the real cause nor the file that caused it.
#
# Deliberately narrow: only the files that must be LF are pinned, so adding
# this does not rewrite every other file in the repo on the next checkout.
*.sub text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
